\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O God of all grace,
\par Thy goodness we praise;
\par Thy Son Thou hast given 
\par to die in our place.
\par He came from above
\par Our curse to remove;
\par He hath loved, He hath loved us:
\par because He would love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Love moved Him to die,
\par And on this we rely;
\par He hath loved, He hath loved us:
\par we cannot tell why;
\par But this we can tell,
\par He hath loved us so well
\par As to lay down His life
\par to redeem us from hell.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He hath ransomed our race;
\par O how shall we praise
\par Or worthily sing Thy unspeakable grace?
\par Nothing else will we know
\par In our journey below,
\par But singing Thy grace
\par to Thy paradise go.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Nay, and when we remove
\par To Thy presence above,
\par Our heaven shall be still 
\par to sing of Thy love.
\par We all shall commend
\par The love of our Friend,
\par For ever beginning 
\par what never shall end.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

